      "value": "@{5c5df2082c5bb810bde843a5|full_name}: I’ve got just GTX 760 2GB :-) . But before upgrade of the game I used 2560x1440 resolution at 20Mbps bitrate with 5GHz WiFi and I had a 30 fps. Do you believe it :-) ? I’d got 2K resolution at 30 fps using so weak videocard for VR. Can you imagine my disappointment when the fps dropped down to 11 after game updating? I'm very disappointed. I use RiftCat for another VR-games and there I’ve got 2K resolution at 30 fps. VRChat has poor optimization.\n\nIf you use WiFi for connection I recommend you also use wireless gamepad instead of mouse and keyboard, and also wireless audio headset. Total freedom of movement :-) . But you cannot use hand gestures in this case because gamepad’s not supported it yet.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
